            "pdfFlavor": "NON_ENGLISH",
            "detectedLanguage": "fr",
            "pageCount": 1,
            "processed": true,
            "summary": "This document is an adverse effect report concerning a male patient, aged 38, who experienced a skin rash and significant itching after taking Ferbolex, a medication administered at a dose of 500 mg twice a day, orally. The treatment started on July 14, 2026, and ended on July 18, 2026. The adverse reactions began on July 17, 2026, and resolved after the medication was stopped. The attending physician, Dr. Lucas Moreau, from France, noted that the patient had no notable medical history, and the severity of the adverse reaction is classified as non-severe, with specific criteria not applicable. \n\nGiven that this document reports a direct adverse effect related to a pharmaceutical product, it is relevant to a patient-safety review. It highlights a potential risk associated with Ferbolex and the patient's experience with the medication, which could be important for future assessments of the drug's safety profile. The resolution of the symptoms upon discontinuation of the medication is also significant, indicating a likely causal relationship between the product and the adverse effect. This information could assist in evaluating the safety and quality of the medication in question.",
            "extractionConfidence": 0.9,
            "translatedText": "--- page 1 ---\nAdverse Effect Report  \nPatient  \nAge: 38  \nSex: Male  \nMedical History: No notable medical history  \nNotifier  \nName: Dr. Lucas Moreau  \nRole: Attending physician  \nCountry: France  \nProduct  \nName: Ferbolex  \nDose: 500 mg twice a day  \nRoute: Oral  \nStart Date: 2026-07-14  \nEnd Date: 2026-07-18  \nReaction  \nDescription: Skin rash and significant itching  \nOnset: 2026-07-17  \nOutcome: Resolved after treatment was stopped  \nSeverity  \nSevere: No  \nCriteria: Not applicable"
        }
